---
// About, as rendered in the overlay panel and on the standalone /about page.
// Typography matches the panel's post reader so the two read as one publication.
const H2 = "margin:38px 0 14px;font-family:'Zen Maru Gothic',sans-serif;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:700;color:var(--pc-head);letter-spacing:-0.01em";
const P = "font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.68;color:var(--pc-body);margin:0 0 20px;text-wrap:pretty";
const A = 'color:var(--pc-accent);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:2px';
---

<div style="width:100%;max-width:760px;padding-bottom:60px">
  <h1 style="margin:0 0 12px;font-family:'Zen Maru Gothic',sans-serif;font-size:clamp(30px,4vw,40px);line-height:1.15;font-weight:700;color:var(--pc-head);letter-spacing:-0.015em">About me</h1>
  <p style="margin:0 0 34px;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--pc-soft);max-width:620px;text-wrap:pretty">
    I build things with AI agents to find out where they actually hold up. Most of it is about
    making learning fun and open to anyone who wants it.
  </p>
  <div style="height:1px;background:var(--pc-line);margin:0 0 30px"></div>

  <p style={P}>
    Most of what gets said about AI comes from people selling something. I'm not selling
    anything. I'd rather find out for myself, so I build real projects with it and write down
    what broke. That's what this site is for.
  </p>

  <h2 style={H2}>What I'm making</h2>
  <p style={P}>
    The big one right now is <strong style="color:var(--pc-strong)">I Love My Evening Television</strong>,
    a series of half-hour films made by crews of Claude agents from one prompt each. Every episode
    starts as a calm little programme and turns strange at minute 20. The first two are on
    YouTube, and <a href="/courses/i-love-my-evening-television/" style={A}>the lore course</a>
    keeps track of the whole world.
  </p>
  <p style={P}>
    <strong style="color:var(--pc-strong)">The Hidden Curriculum</strong> is a free video course
    on the small stuff nobody tells you when you start building with AI, like what a folder path
    is. Agents write, fact-check, narrate and animate every lesson.
    <a href="/courses/the-hidden-curriculum/" style={A}>Start it here</a>.
  </p>
  <p style={P}>
    Then there are my original characters. <strong style="color:var(--pc-strong)">Jefrie</strong>,
    <strong style="color:var(--pc-strong)">BloodTailor</strong> and the rest of the cast keep
    showing up in everything I make. They get drawn, painted in oil, animated and dropped into games.
  </p>
  <p style={P}>
    On the game side there's <strong style="color:var(--pc-strong)">BLACKWATER</strong>, zombies
    but you're cave diving, which I built in a weekend and you can play in your browser. And
    <strong style="color:var(--pc-strong)">LLM Monster Hunter</strong>, a monster-catching game
    where no monster exists until you meet it. The AI writes, paints and referees each one while
    the code keeps every number. It's paused for now. Everything else is on
    <a href="/projects" style={A}>the projects page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 style={H2}>Why I write it down</h2>
  <p style={P}>
    <a href="/ledger" style={A}>The ledger</a> is where I file what I tried and what came of it,
    dead ends included. The prompt that seemed obviously right and wasn't. The agent that did
    something so strange I had to screenshot it. If you're learning this stuff too, I think an
    honest write-up of a failure is worth more than another launch announcement.
  </p>

  <h2 style={H2}>Away from the keyboard</h2>
  <p style={P}>
    I'm learning Japanese and I volunteer with a local Japanese club, including a bilingual
    Studio Ghibli storytime. I play fingerstyle guitar and write songs. I'm also in Toastmasters,
    which has done more for my writing than any style guide.
  </p>

  <h2 style={H2}>Say hello</h2>
  <p style={P}>
    If you're building something close to any of this, or you just want to talk about where
    agents break, I'd like to hear from you.
    Email <a href="mailto:Aaronjorelup@gmail.com" style={A}>Aaronjorelup@gmail.com</a>, or find
    me on <a href="https://github.com/aaronorelup" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" style={A}>GitHub</a>
    and <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/aaron-orelup/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" style={A}>LinkedIn</a>.
  </p>
</div>
